   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "prop:mean-based-bandit-algorithm",
    "number": "Proposition 3",
    "quote": "Let $\\eta_t$, $\\epsilon_t$ be decreasing sequences with $\\epsilon_t \\in \\omega(\\sqrt{\\log(t)/t})$ and let $p > 0$. The algorithm is $\\gamma_t$-mean-based with rate $\\max\\{\\eta_t, \\epsilon_t\\} + \\frac{k \\cdot \\sqrt{\\log(t)}}{\\epsilon_t \\cdot \\sqrt{t}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2 p} + \\frac{1}{t^p}$. For $\\eta_t \\leq \\epsilon_t = \\min\\{1, \\sqrt[4]{\\log(t) / t}\\}$ and $t$ such that $\\epsilon_t < 1$, this implies $\\gamma_t = (1 + \\sqrt{2p} \\cdot k) \\cdot \\sqrt[4]{\\frac{{\\log(t)}}{t}} + \\frac{1}{t^p}$"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Bound is on the mean-based rate gamma_t (the probability of playing a dominated action at round t+1 and the dominance threshold), not regret. General form: max{eta_t,eps_t} + k sqrt(2p log t)/(eps_t sqrt t) + t^{-p}. Probability type is not a standard category; it is a per-round probability bound."
  },
